From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:37:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bundle a GBA BIOS that can actually be detected

The bundled open-source BIOS was an old Cult-of-GBA build predating their
PR #16, whose RegisterRamReset is missing the SIO branch. Emerald calls
RegisterRamReset at startup, and that branch is what writes JOY_TRANS,
which is what sets the JOY-bus status bit the GameCube's JoyBoot ladder
requires. Without it the status byte stays 0x00, the ladder aborts before
transferring anything, and the game never detects the GBA -- the field
telemetry showed exactly that: link windows opening, thousands of probes,
zero handshakes.

The literal 0x04000120 (the SIO register base the reset writes) is absent
from the old bundled image, present in the official dump at 0x2c10, and
present in the current Cult-of-GBA build at 0x1098. Replace the bundled
image with that build (upstream a30e9a9, the merge of the register-ram-reset
fix; MIT licensed, redistributable) and restore it as the fallback when the
user has no official dump.

The previous revision routed the no-official-dump case to mGBA's HLE BIOS
on harness evidence. On device that behaved exactly like the old bundled
build, so the harness result did not hold; an actual BIOS image is used
again. Being bundled, it is byte-identical on every client, which keeps
netplay deterministic when no player has an official dump.
---
 Data/Sys/GBA/gba_bios.bin       | Bin 16384 -> 16384 bytes
 Source/Core/Core/HW/GBACore.cpp |  23 ++++++++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Data/Sys/GBA/gba_bios.bin b/Data/Sys/GBA/gba_bios.bin
index 802982e4336f04eebc08148ffaf904d19ecd0ba4..ec03b9e3a00b7723f3f3594828d99156af230341 100644
GIT binary patch
